To implement this, we need to shift from showing only "Pending Since" for the current stage to showing a historical "Duration" for every completed stage in the workflow.
### 1. Backend: Calculate Durations for All Stages
We need a new service method to calculate the duration of *each* step based on the VOUCHER_WORKFLOW table logs.
**In VoucherQueryService.java**, add this method:
```java
public List<Map<String, String>> getStageDurations(String batchId) {
    // Fetches every action and its timestamp in order
    String sql = "SELECT LAST_ACTION, LAST_ACTION_AT FROM VOUCHER_WORKFLOW WHERE BATCH_ID_FK = ? ORDER BY LAST_ACTION_AT ASC";
    List<Map<String, Object>> history = jdbcTemplate.queryForList(sql, batchId);
    List<Map<String, String>> durations = new ArrayList<>();

    for (int i = 0; i < history.size() - 1; i++) {
        LocalDateTime start = ((Timestamp) history.get(i).get("LAST_ACTION_AT")).toLocalDateTime();
        LocalDateTime end = ((Timestamp) history.get(i + 1).get("LAST_ACTION_AT")).toLocalDateTime();
        Duration d = Duration.between(start, end);
        
        Map<String, String> entry = new HashMap<>();
        entry.put("action", (String) history.get(i).get("LAST_ACTION"));
        entry.put("duration", d.toHours() + "h " + d.toMinutesPart() + "m");
        durations.add(entry);
    }
    return durations;
}

```
